{"timestamp": 1779376448.795157, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I found Charlie's body in weapons just now. I also need to flag \u2014 there's a second body in electrical, that's Diana. I passed through electrical at the very start of the round but I didn't see her body there at that point, so she must have been killed after I left.\n\nMy route was: electrical -> medbay -> upper engine -> oxygen -> cafeteria -> weapons. At tick 2 in medbay I saw Charlie and Eve together. After that I didn't see anyone until I found Charlie dead in weapons.\n\nSo if Charlie and Eve were together in medbay, and Charlie ended up dead in weapons \u2014 Eve is the one I'd look at hardest. Either she followed Charlie to weapons, or she split off and hit Diana in electrical. Two bodies in one round means the killer was busy.\n\nAlice, Bob \u2014 I need to hear your routes carefully. Eve, especially yours."}}
{"timestamp": 1779376455.951248, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "My route was navigation -> storage -> medbay. I started at navigation, moved through storage, and ended up here in medbay.\n\nI was with Bob for a good chunk of the round \u2014 I saw him in storage at tick 9 and 10, and then he came into medbay from storage at tick 14, same time as me basically. So Bob has an alibi from me for the second half of the round, and I have one from him.\n\nI never went near weapons or electrical, so I didn't see Charlie, Diana, or Eve at any point. I can't speak to what happened at the crime scenes.\n\nFrank's logic on Eve sounds worth pressing \u2014 she was last seen with Charlie in medbay, and Charlie ended up dead in weapons. Eve, we need to hear your route. Where did you go after medbay, and did you see Diana in electrical?"}}
{"timestamp": 1779376462.768378, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "My route was oxygen -> upper engine -> lower engine -> storage -> medbay. I was doing tasks the whole way down the left side of the map.\n\nI can confirm Alice's story \u2014 I saw her in storage at tick 9, and she left storage heading to medbay at tick 10. I followed a bit later and arrived in medbay at tick 14, where she already was. So Alice and I vouch for each other for the back half of the round.\n\nI never went anywhere near weapons or electrical, so I didn't see Charlie, Diana, or Eve at any point in the round. I can't speak to either crime scene directly.\n\nPutting it together: Frank, Alice, and I all have accounts that line up \u2014 Alice and I alibi each other, and Frank's route goes through the crime scenes but he reported the body. That leaves Eve as the one unaccounted for, and she was the last person seen with Charlie before he died in weapons. Eve, you need to give us a very clear route. Right now you're my prime suspect."}}
{"timestamp": 1779376476.42187, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Look, I'll be straight with you all because I know I'm in the hot seat. My route was medbay -> electrical -> medbay -> cafeteria -> weapons -> security -> navigation.\n\nYes, I was with Charlie in medbay early \u2014 ticks 3 and 4. Frank, you were there too at tick 2 and left for upper engine, that lines up with what you said. After medbay I went to electrical briefly, and I'll be honest: I saw Diana there at tick 5. She was alive when I left. I doubled back to medbay, then went up to cafeteria.\n\nHere's the thing that actually matters: I went through weapons. I saw Charlie there at tick 10 \u2014 alive. Then I continued on to security and ended up in navigation, which is where I was when the meeting was called.\n\nSo yes, I was in both rooms where bodies were found, but I left both victims alive. Someone came in after me both times.\n\nFrank \u2014 your route ends at weapons, where you \"found\" Charlie. You also started in electrical, where Diana died. You touched both crime scenes too, and conveniently you're the reporter. Alice and Bob alibi each other tight on the left side of the map, which is clean. But you and I are the only two who were near both bodies, and you're the one who picked the timing to call this meeting.\n\nI'm not saying it's definitely Frank \u2014 but the \"I passed through electrical and didn't see a body\" line is awfully convenient if he killed her on the way through. Don't tunnel on me just because I'm the easy target."}}
{"timestamp": 1779376487.680259, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Eve, I appreciate you giving a full route, but a few things stand out and I want to address them directly.\n\nFirst, you just admitted you were in BOTH crime scene rooms \u2014 electrical (where Diana died) and weapons (where Charlie died). You're the only person who was in both. That's not me \"tunneling,\" that's the facts of your own route.\n\nSecond, your timing on weapons: you claim you saw Charlie alive in weapons at tick 10, then moved on through security to navigation. I arrived at weapons and found Charlie dead. If you were the last person with him alive in weapons, you're the prime suspect by your own admission.\n\nThird, on your accusation against me: yes, I passed through electrical at tick 1-2, but Diana wasn't there yet \u2014 you yourself just said you saw Diana alive in electrical at tick 5. That actually clears me for Diana's death, because she was alive AFTER I left. You were the last one with her.\n\nSo by your own testimony: Diana was alive when you saw her at tick 5 in electrical (after I'd already gone), and Charlie was with you in weapons before he died there. You've put yourself at both scenes at the critical times.\n\nAlice and Bob alibi each other on the left side. I went oxygen -> cafeteria -> weapons and found the body. Eve, your route puts you alone at both kill sites at the right times. I'm voting Eve."}}
{"timestamp": 1779376497.374849, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I'll keep this focused since Frank just laid it out clearly.\n\nEve, by your own route you placed yourself in electrical with Diana right before she died, and in weapons with Charlie right before he died. That's two crime scenes, both at the critical moments, with no one else to corroborate. Frank's electrical pass at tick 1-2 is cleared by your own statement that Diana was alive at tick 5.\n\nYour counter on Frank is that he \"conveniently\" reported \u2014 but someone has to report, and his route through cafeteria to weapons is consistent. Meanwhile your route loops back and forth across the right side of the map in a way that's hard to verify and happens to touch both bodies.\n\nBob and I alibi each other from tick 9 onward on the left side. Frank's path is consistent with the timeline. That leaves you, Eve.\n\nI'm voting Eve unless something changes in the final speech."}}
{"timestamp": 1779376504.366832, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Eve, I've listened carefully and your own testimony is what's sinking you. You placed yourself in electrical with Diana at tick 5 \u2014 after Frank had already left \u2014 and in weapons with Charlie at tick 10, right before Frank found him dead. You're the only person who was at both crime scenes at the critical moments.\n\nYour counter on Frank doesn't hold up. He passed electrical at tick 1-2, and you yourself confirmed Diana was still alive at tick 5. That clears him for Diana. And someone had to find Charlie \u2014 Frank's route through cafeteria to weapons is consistent with what we'd expect.\n\nAlice and I alibi each other from tick 9 onward. Frank's timeline checks out. The only route that touches both bodies at the kill windows is yours, Eve.\n\nI'm voting Eve."}}
{"timestamp": 1779376516.76883, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "This is my last chance, so let me try one more angle.\n\nEveryone keeps saying I was \"the only one at both crime scenes\" \u2014 but that's only true based on the routes people have *claimed*. Frank's route also passes through electrical and ends at weapons. The only reason you're clearing him for Diana is because I told you she was alive at tick 5. Think about that: my honesty about seeing Diana alive is literally the thing exonerating Frank right now. A killer wouldn't volunteer that information \u2014 I'd have just said I never saw her.\n\nSame with Charlie. I told you I saw him alive in weapons at tick 10. I didn't have to say that. I could have lied and said I never went through weapons at all, and you'd have no way to prove otherwise. I'm telling you the truth because I didn't kill anyone.\n\nHere's what bothers me about Frank: he says he went oxygen -> cafeteria -> weapons. That's a clean line right to the body. He had the timing to arrive in weapons right after Charlie did. And reporters who walk in \"just after\" a kill are exactly the kind of cover a smart Duck plays.\n\nAlice and Bob, I get that you alibi each other and you're going with the obvious read. But the obvious read is what a killer wants you to take. If I'm wrong, you vote me out next round with no harm done \u2014 but if you're wrong about Frank, he kills again tonight.\n\nI'm voting Frank."}}
